E. E2 pairs at a FIXED difference d
   (i) pure shifts, E2 values used directly: target graph {i~j : |h_i-h_j| = d} is bipartite
       (colour h by floor(h/d) mod 2), so blocked for every tuple.  Exhaustive check, shifts in [0,24]:
       25123 tuples (k=2..4, d in {1,2,4,6,12}) with an edge: 0 not blocked
   (ii) multipliers: X = c*L(m) is E2 if c = 1 and L(m) is E2, or c = prime and L(m) is prime.
        Triple m, m+6, m+12: 2(m+6)-2m = 12, 2(m+12)-2(m+6) = 12, (m+12)-m = 12.
        target: (m, m+6) both prime, or (m+6, m+12) both prime, or (m, m+12) both E2;
        each event gives x, x+12 both E2 (for m > 2):
        admissible {m, m+6, m+12}: (True, None)
  triangle {0,6,12}: PR-PR, PR-PR, E2-E2                         k=3 UNBLOCKED  c=['1', '-1', '1'] c0=0 margin=1/2  [as predicted]
        signed-cycle lemma: an edge (i,j) using multipliers (c_i,c_j) needs c_i a_i = c_j a_j, and
        forbids the signs s_i = (-1)^Omega(c_i), s_j = (-1)^Omega(c_j); so s_i s_j = (-1)^(Omega(a_i)+Omega(a_j))
        and the product of s_i s_j around any cycle is +1.  Check: all signed graphs on 3 and 4
        vertices (one forbidden sign pair per edge): blocked <=> the system eps_i eps_j = -s_i s_j is
        solvable (switching-balanced), and hence, for cycle products +1, <=> the graph is bipartite:
        n=3: 125 signed graphs, 0 mismatches
        n=4: 15625 signed graphs, 0 mismatches
   (iii) search: admissible triples of forms a_i m + b_i (a_1 <= 12, a_2, a_3 <= 72) and multipliers in
        {1,2,3,5,7,11,13} such that EVERY pair (i,j) has an identity c_i L_i - c_j L_j = +-d
        (a triangle, hence unblocked by (ii)).  Smallest example per d:
        d= 1: none in range
        d= 2: none in range
        d= 4: none in range
        d= 6: none in range
        d= 8: none in range
        d=12: L=(1m+0, 1m+12, 1m+6)  mult (1,2)=(1, 1) (1,3)=(2, 2) (2,3)=(2, 2)  [L1,L2 E2,E2; L1,L3 prime,prime; L2,L3 prime,prime]

