G. GGPY's own sieve functional vs the class (0609615 Thms 7-8, (8.1)): the method gives nu+1 E2
   among k forms iff rho = k(k-1)(J1+J2+J3)/(B J0) > nu for some polynomial P.  The class blocks
   'nu+1 of k E2' iff k <= 2 nu, so consistency requires max_P rho <= ceil(k/2) (heuristically <= k/2).
   rho is a ratio of quadratic forms in the coefficients of P (deg <= D): generalized eigenvalue,
   Gauss-Legendre quadrature (floating point, not a certificate).
   check vs paper (Thm 2: k=3, B=4, eta=1/144, P=1+6x): J0 = 2.533333 (paper 38/15 = 2.533333), rho = 1.000065 > 1
   B=4      eta=0, D<=6  max rho  k=2:0.7576  k=3:1.0039  k=4:1.2078  k=5:1.3823  k=6:1.5351  k=7:1.6711  k=8:1.7938
   B=3      eta=0, D<=6  max rho  k=2:0.8604  k=3:1.1645  k=4:1.4194  k=5:1.6390  k=6:1.8323  k=7:2.0049  k=8:2.1611
   B=2.0001 eta=0, D<=6  max rho  k=2:0.9614  k=3:1.3629  k=4:1.7090  k=5:2.0115  k=6:2.2801  k=7:2.5214  k=8:2.7407
   max over the table of rho/(k/2) = 0.9614  (< 1: no case blocked by the class is reached)
